      "message": "Since we no longer deduplicate dependencies with `SmallSet` here and now push duplicate entries into `Target::starlark_deps_` to be consumed positionally, could we add a case to `integration_tests/starlark/` where the same target is referenced multiple times (e.g., across two attributes or multiple keys in a label dict)?\n\nRight now `FakeTargetRef::deps()` in unit tests still resolves via `session.get_target()`, so an integration test covering duplicates would lock in the end-to-end C++ `starlark_deps_` ↔ Rust positional resolution contract.",
